FAQ = [
 ("What is the best LED light upgrade for a 2025–2026 4Runner?",
  "For most non-TRD Pro trucks, Baja Designs' S2 Sport fog light replacement kit. Baja lists four S2 Sport lights at 1,581 lumens and 12.4 watts each, with brackets, hardware and splitter harnesses, designed to run from the stock fog switch, for 2025–2026 4Runners that are not TRD Pro. It costs $606.95 at Baja. It keeps a factory look and low glare. If you want reach rather than width, add hood-hinge ditch pods; a true light bar on the 6th gen is still mostly a TRD Pro and Trailhunter grille upgrade sold maker-direct."),
 ("Do 2010–2024 4Runner light bar brackets fit the 2025 4Runner?",
  "No. The 2025 4Runner moved to Toyota's TNGA-F platform, shared with the Tacoma, Tundra, Land Cruiser and Sequoia, and the front end, hood and roof are all new. Cali Raised says its 2025+ ditch kit is not designed for 2024 or older models, and its 5th-gen grille and roof brackets are listed only to 2024. Buy parts whose listing names 2025 or 2026. Some 6th-gen parts are shared with the 2024+ Tacoma and 2022+ Tundra instead, which is why several listings name all three."),
 ("Does the 2025 4Runner come with a factory light bar?",
  "Only certain trims. Toyota's launch release says the TRD Pro gets a 20 in LED light bar integrated into a heritage-inspired TOYOTA grille plus RIGID Industries LED fog lamps, and the Trailhunter gets RIGID color-selectable LED fog lamps, an ARB roof rack and a bronze TOYOTA grille with an integrated LED light bar. Toyota also lists LED head and fog lights on the SR5. The release names a light bar on those two grades only, and we could not confirm whether any other grade has one, so look at your grille. Where there is no factory bar, an add-on bar needs its own brackets, harness and switch."),
 ("Why are there so few light bar kits for the 6th-gen 4Runner?",
  "Because the truck is new and the front end is new. The 2010–2024 4Runner ran 15 years and built up grille, fog-pocket, hood-hinge and roof kits from many brands. The 6th gen went on sale in late 2024, and makers have started with the easy mounts: fog pockets and hood-hinge ditch brackets. Grille bar kits so far target the TRD Pro and Trailhunter grille, and the ones we found sell maker-direct. Expect the list to grow; until then, buy only parts that name 2025 or 2026."),
 ("Are LED light bars and ditch lights legal on a 4Runner?",
  "Usually only off-road. Rules vary by state, but many treat light bars, ditch pods and other auxiliary lights with off-road beams as off-road equipment that must be switched off on public roads, and some require an opaque cover or limit how many auxiliary lamps you can run. Fog lights sold to an SAE fog standard are the easiest to keep street-friendly; Baja sells an S2 SAE version of its 6th-gen fog kit for that reason. Check your own state's rules before driving with any auxiliary light on."),
 ("Will Baja's fog kit fit a TRD Pro or Trailhunter?",
  "Not the one on this page. Baja says its S2 Sport fog light replacement kit will not work on TRD Pro models, and retailers list its S2 SAE version as non-TRD Pro and non-Trailhunter. Both of those trims already come with RIGID fog lamps from the factory, per Toyota. For those trucks, the upgrade path is the grille: Diode Dynamics sells an SS20 grille light bar kit for 2025+ 4Runners with the OEM TRD Pro or Trailhunter grille, maker-direct."),
 ("Do I need to drill to add lights to a 2025 4Runner?",
  "Not with the kits on this page. Cali Raised describes its 2025+ ditch kit as bolt-on at existing factory mounting points, typically one to two hours with basic hand tools. Its fog replacement kit and Baja's S2 kit use the factory fog pockets and need no cutting or drilling per the makers. Diode Dynamics' ditch kit uses factory mounting points too, per RealTruck. Where drilling can come in is routing a harness through the firewall or adding a switch, so read the install sheet first."),
 ("How many amps will extra lights draw on a 2025 4Runner?",
  "Divide watts by system voltage. Baja lists each S2 Sport light at 12.4 W and 0.9 A, so its four-light kit draws about 3.6 A. A pair of Cali Raised 18 W ditch pods draws roughly 2.6 A at 13.8 V, and its two 30 W fog bars roughly 4.3 A. Diode's SS20 grille bar is listed at 76.5 W (Sport) or 105 W (Pro), or roughly 5.5 A to 7.6 A. Fuse and relay each circuit for its own load."),
 ("Can I run a roof light bar on the 2025 4Runner?",
  "Yes, but the mount comes from the rack, not the truck. The 6th gen has a new roof and rail geometry, and the Trailhunter wears a factory ARB platform. Aftermarket 6th-gen platforms, such as the ones on our roof rack page, are where light bar brackets attach, and whether a given rack offers a light mount varies by maker. A roof bar gives the most reach but bounces the most glare off the hood, adds wind noise at highway speed and is off-road lighting in practically every state. Choose the rack first, then a bar and brackets that rack maker lists."),
 ("Should I pick amber or white ditch and fog lights?",
  "Amber for dust, rain and snow; white for maximum visible output. Amber light scatters less off particles in the air, so it causes less back-glare in bad weather, which is why most fog and ditch kits on this page are offered in both. Baja offers Baja Amber and clear lenses on its S2 kit, Cali Raised offers amber or white on its fog kit and amber 3x2 pods on its ditch kit. Many owners run amber low on the truck and white higher up."),
]

